          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21046 utils: lhsmtool_posix daemon exits once registered",
        "message": "LU-21046 utils: lhsmtool_posix daemon exits once registered\n\n\"lhsmtool_posix --daemon\" forked with daemon() before registering as\na copytool, so the command returned while the copytool was not yet\nable to receive requests.  sanity-hsm tests start the copytool and\nthen stop it with SIGSTOP to keep requests in STARTED state.  If the\nsignal arrived before llapi_hsm_copytool_register(), the copytool was\nnever registered, the request stayed WAITING, and e.g. test_251\nfailed with \"request ... is not STARTED on mds1\".\n\nMake the parent wait until the child has registered, and exit with\nan error if the child exits before that.  \"--daemon\" now waits for\nthe MDTs to answer the registration, and reports a startup failure,\ne.g. a pid file held by another copytool, with a non-zero exit.\n\nRemove the second copytool started by sanity-hsm test_31a, test_260b\nand test_260c while the first one was still running.  It always\nfailed to lock the pid file and exited, which is now an error.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-hsm\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I4a54758104c996e30482089a5651ee1f0d3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
